### 5.2 Bytes moved are not the cost

No attempt to make the tier faster by moving fewer bytes closed its gap to the full cache:

| Change | Result |
|---|---|
| Twice the VRAM slots, far fewer on-demand fetches | slightly faster |
| Layer-ahead prefetch hiding the copies inside compute | slower than synchronous fetch |
| int8 warm/cold tier, half the bytes on the wire | {{ phase5.analysis.summary.latency_ratio_at.b25 | .2f }}× slower |
| Remove the per-layer host sync (replay ablation) | {{ phase11.ceiling.summary.ceiling_speedup.min | .2f }}–{{ phase11.ceiling.summary.ceiling_speedup.max | .2f }}× faster: the ceiling |
| Move no KV at all: attend to cold blocks on the CPU | {{ phase7.analysis.summary.over_approx.min | .2f }}–{{ phase7.analysis.summary.over_approx.max | .2f }}× slower than the tier it extends, and exact |

At a 25% budget the tier moves {{ phase5.analysis.summary.fetch_mib_at.b25.exact | .1f }} MiB per
token, under a millisecond of link time, while choosing what to move costs
{{ phase5.ceiling.summary.host_select_ms.min | .0f }}–{{ phase5.ceiling.summary.host_select_ms.max | .0f }} ms.
Each selecting layer must bring its top-K indices to the host before it can issue the fetch, and
the context sweep shows that round trip is a per-layer constant: at least
{{ phase8.analysis.summary.manager_intercept_share.min | pct0 }} of the selecting rungs' manager cost
sits at zero blocks ranked. The replay ablation, which removes the decision while fetching identical
blocks, bounds what a device-side decision could recover: its fastest decode,
{{ phase11.ceiling.summary.replay_ms.min | .1f }} ms per token, is still slower than the full cache's
{{ phase11.ceiling.summary.full_decode_ms | .1f }} ms. On this machine, a tier narrows the gap to
keeping KV in VRAM and never closes it, at any context measured.

### 5.3 Context length: the fraction is what transfers

Sweeping {{ phase8.analysis.summary.contexts_measured | int }} contexts for rungs 2, 5, 6 and 9 shows
accuracy is set by the budget *fraction*: matched at a fraction, retention spreads
{{ phase8.analysis.summary.collapse_k_over_fraction | .1f }}× less across contexts than matched at a
constant number of selected blocks, the parameterization Quest uses. A constant token budget
therefore does not carry from one context to another.

